    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d136-a1-a5">

                <pb facs="0472" n="414" xml:id="pg414"/>


                <head>Department of Foreign Relations and Government–Government Branch–Section
                    first.</head>
                <p>Trusting to your patriotism, and as a reward for your services, the citizen
                    President of the republic has been pleased to appoint you governor of the State
                    of Tamaulipas. I send you instructions in another paper, ordering you to repair
                    to that territory without delay, to begin the duties of your office. I enclose
                    this despatch to citizen General José M. de J. Carvajal, former governor of that
                    State, for his instruction.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left">Independence and liberty!
                            <placeName>Chihuahua</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1866-08-07">August 7, 1866</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>LERDO DE TEJADA.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Citizen General <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago Tapia</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Governor of the State of Tamaulipas</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
